<tr><td>statement inside switch with no case/default</td><td>valid</td><td>CE</td></tr>
<tr><td>case y with int y = 20</td><td>valid</td><td>CE constant expression required</td></tr>
<tr><td>case y with final int y; then y = 20;</td><td>valid because final</td><td>CE — not a compile-time constant</td></tr>
<tr><td>case y with final Integer y = 10</td><td>valid</td><td>CE constant expression required</td></tr>
<tr><td>byte b; case 1000</td><td>valid (promoted to int)</td><td>CE possible loss of precision</td></tr>
<tr><td>switch(b+1) { case 1000 }</td><td>same CE</td><td>valid — argument is int</td></tr>
<tr><td>case 97 and case &#x27;a&#x27;</td><td>both valid</td><td>CE duplicate case label</td></tr>
<tr><td>default first, x matches a later case</td><td>default always runs</td><td>jump to the matching case; default skipped</td></tr>
<tr><td>default first, no match, no break</td><td>only default prints</td><td>default and following cases until break</td></tr>
<tr><td>Integer i = null; switch(i)</td><td>default / CE</td><td>compiles; NPE</td></tr>
<tr><td>String s = null; switch(s)</td><td>default</td><td>compiles; NPE</td></tr>
<tr><td>case Beer.KF</td><td>valid</td><td>CE — must be unqualified KF</td></tr>
<tr><td>new String(&quot;durga&quot;) vs case &quot;durga&quot;</td><td>not matched (==)</td><td>matched (equals)</td></tr>
<tr><td>&quot;Hyderabad&quot; vs &quot;hyderabad&quot;</td><td>same</td><td>different labels; case-sensitive</td></tr>
<tr><td>two int y in two cases</td><td>valid</td><td>CE — y already defined in this switch</td></tr>
